## CRC Library Missing Error

### Symptom
The `arm_controller` node crashes with:
```
OSError: /usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/unitree_sdk2py/utils/lib/crc_amd64.so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory
```

### Cause
The SDK's native CRC library wasn't copied during installation.

### Solution

Copy the missing library directory from your working SDK:

```bash
cp -r /unitree_sdk2_python_local/unitree_sdk2py/utils/lib /usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/unitree_sdk2py/utils/
```

Verify:
```bash
ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/unitree_sdk2py/utils/lib/
```

You should see `crc_amd64.so` (or `crc_arm64.so` on ARM systems).

